{"content":[{"c":["ELIPHAZ"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Oldest son of Esau and his wife Adah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.4-16","r":"Gen.36.4-16","rawR":"Gen.36.4-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.4-16","value":"Gen.36.4-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:4-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.35-36","r":"1Chr.1.35-36","rawR":"1Chr.1.35-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.35-36","value":"1Chr.1.35-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:35-36"},"). He was the ancestor of a number of Edomite clans."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of Job’s friends, called the Temanite (see ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.49.7","r":"Jer.49.7","rawR":"Jer.49.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.49.7","value":"Jer.49.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 49:7"},"). Teman was traditionally associated with wisdom; hence Eliphaz’s speech depicts the orthodox view of sin and punishment. His three addresses (",{"href":"?bref=Job.4.1-21","r":"Job.4.1-21","rawR":"Job.4.1-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.4.1-21","value":"Job.4.1-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Job.15.1-35","r":"Job.15.1-35","rawR":"Job.15.1-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.15.1-35","value":"Job.15.1-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"15"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Job.22.1-30","r":"Job.22.1-30","rawR":"Job.22.1-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.22.1-30","value":"Job.22.1-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"22"},") failed to grapple with the essence of Job’s problem because he assumed previous major sin in Job’s life."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JobBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JobBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JobBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Job, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"sp","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eliphaz","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 36:4-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.4-16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.4-16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.4-16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:35-36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.35-36","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.35-36","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.35-36"},{"anchorText":"Jer 49:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.49.7","rawQueryValue":"Jer.49.7","sourceRefExact":"Jer.49.7"},{"anchorText":"Jb 4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.4.1-21","rawQueryValue":"Job.4.1-21","sourceRefExact":"Job.4.1-21"},{"anchorText":"15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.15.1-35","rawQueryValue":"Job.15.1-35","sourceRefExact":"Job.15.1-35"},{"anchorText":"22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.22.1-30","rawQueryValue":"Job.22.1-30","sourceRefExact":"Job.22.1-30"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e160f067e2f9db9ed24c261c41ef047720f1fbef92a75d949dbc4dc09b3dcff9","sourceItemName":"Eliphaz","sourceItemOrder":109,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Eliphaz","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Eliphaz","title":"Eliphaz","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}